                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_190\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit (in TripleAPlayer.java's move() method) splits a single, incorrectly-merged\nif-condition into two separate if-blocks so that the combat-move sound\n(SoundPath.CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_COMBAT) and the non-combat-move sound\n(SoundPath.CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_NONCOMBAT) are each played correctly for their respective phase.\nBefore the fix, the buggy code read:\n\n    if ((nonCombat && !m_soundPlayedAlreadyNonCombatMove) || (!nonCombat && !m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove)) {\n      ClipPlayer.play(SoundPath.CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_NONCOMBAT, id);\n      m_soundPlayedAlreadyNonCombatMove = true;\n    }\n\nThis single combined condition always plays the NON-COMBAT sound clip (and only sets the\nnon-combat \"already played\" flag) even when the game is actually in a COMBAT move phase,\nand it never sets m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove \u2014 so combat moves never get their own sound\nand the flag meant to guard repeated combat-move sound playback is never updated.\n\nTracing the blob hashes through the candidate diffs shows the exact point this bug was\nintroduced. candidate_190 modifies TripleAPlayer.java from blob e7570dbe6 to c009b19c7, and\nin that diff the move-sound logic is changed from two separate, correct if/else-if branches:\n\n    if (nonCombat && !m_soundPlayedAlreadyNonCombatMove) {\n      DefaultSoundChannel.playSoundOnLocalMachine(SoundPath.CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_NONCOMBAT, id.getName());\n      m_soundPlayedAlreadyNonCombatMove = true;\n    } else if (!nonCombat && !m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove) {\n      DefaultSoundChannel.playSoundOnLocalMachine(SoundPath.CLIP_PHASE_MOVE_COMBAT, id.getName());\n      m_soundPlayedAlreadyCombatMove = true;\n    }\n\ninto the single, buggy combined condition shown above (while simultaneously switching the\nsound-playing API from DefaultSoundChannel.playSoundOnLocalMachine back to ClipPlayer.play).\nThis is precisely the erroneous code pattern that the fix commit later corrects by\nre-splitting it into two separate if-blocks (one for nonCombat, one for combat), each with\nits own ClipPlayer.play call and its own \"already played\" flag update.\n\nSubsequent candidate_189 (blob c009b19c7 -> 01443c98b) only changes an unrelated parameter\ntype (id.getName() -> id) and leaves the buggy merged condition untouched, and candidate_191\nis the fix commit itself (01443c98b -> bceb3ed93, identical to fix_commit_diff.txt).\nTherefore candidate_190 is the commit that first introduced the problematic merged\ncondition that caused combat-move sounds to never play correctly.\n"
                }
